1. Kubernetes Observability Stack:
    - A Kubernetes observability stack gives you visibility into metrics, logs, traces, and alerts so you can understand system health, debug problems, and monitor applications.

2. Metrics Monitoring — Prometheus
    - What it does
        Collects time-series metrics from:
            Kubernetes nodes
            Pods
            Containers
            Applications
            Databases
            Ingress controllers
        Common Metrics
            CPU usage
            Memory usage
            Request latency
            Error rates
            Pod restarts
            Node health
        Architecture
            App Pods --> /metrics endpoint --> Prometheus --> Grafana
        Key Components
            Prometheus Server
            kube-state-metrics
            node-exporter
            Alertmanager
            ServiceMonitors
        Install
            Most people use:
                Prometheus Operator (kube-prometheus-stack)
                Prometheus Official Docs
        Example Metric
            http_requests_total
        Example Query
            rate(http_requests_total[5m])

3. Visualization — Grafana
    - What it does
        Grafana visualizes:
            Prometheus metrics
            Logs
            Traces
            Alerts
    - Features
        Dashboards
        Alert panels
        Variables
        Drill-down monitoring
        Correlation between logs + traces + metrics
    - Popular Dashboards
        Kubernetes cluster monitoring
        Node monitoring
        NGINX ingress
        PostgreSQL
        Redis
        Application performance
    - Install
        Grafana Official Site
        Grafana Kubernetes Monitoring
    - Flow
        Prometheus --> Grafana Dashboard

4. Logging Stack
    - Purpose
        Centralized log aggregation from:
            Pods
            Containers
            Nodes
            System services
    - Popular Kubernetes Logging Stacks
        Option A (Most Popular)
            EFK Stack
                Elasticsearch
                Fluent Bit / Fluentd
                Kibana
            Flow
                Pods --> Fluent Bit --> Elasticsearch --> Kibana
        Option B (Modern + Lightweight)
            Loki Stack
                Recommended for Kubernetes beginners.
            Components:
                Loki
                Promtail
                Grafana
            Flow
                Pods --> Promtail --> Loki --> Grafana
        - Why Loki?
            Cheap storage
            Lightweight
            Native Grafana integration
            Easier than Elasticsearch
        - Install
            Grafana Loki
            Loki Helm Charts

5. Distributed Tracing
    - Purpose
        Tracks requests across microservices.
    - Example:
        Frontend --> API --> Auth Service --> DB
    - Tracing shows:
        Request path
        Latency per service
        Bottlenecks
        Failures
    - Popular Tracing Tools
        Jaeger
            Created by Uber.
        Tempo
            Grafana’s tracing backend.
        OpenTelemetry
            Industry standard instrumentation framework.
        Recommended Modern Stack
            OpenTelemetry + Tempo + Grafana
        Flow
            Apps
            ↓
            OpenTelemetry SDK
            ↓
            OpenTelemetry Collector
            ↓
            Tempo / Jaeger
            ↓
            Grafana
        Install
            OpenTelemetry Docs
            Grafana Tempo
            Jaeger Docs

6. Alerting
    - Purpose
        Notify when something goes wrong.
    - Examples:
        High CPU
        Pod crash loops
        Memory spikes
        HTTP 500 increase
        Node down
    - Alerting Flow
        Prometheus --> Alertmanager --> Slack/Email/PagerDuty
    - Components
        Prometheus alert rules
        Alertmanager
        Notification channels
    - Example Rule
        groups:
        - name: high-cpu
            rules:
            - alert: HighCPUUsage
                expr: cpu_usage > 80
                for: 5m
    - Install
        Alertmanager Docs

